      url: "https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/26/219",
      excerpt: `${amountsNote} Phase-out per \xA7 219(g)(2): the limit is reduced by the amount bearing the same ratio to it as excess MAGI bears to $10,000 ($20,000 joint), the reduction "rounded to the next lowest $10"; the limit is not reduced "below $200 unless\u2026 reduced to zero." MAGI is AGI without regard to \xA7\xA7 221 and 219 (\xA7 219(g)(3)(A)). Deduction capped at includible compensation (\xA7 219(b)(1)(B)) \u2014 compensation \u2248 wages + SE earnings net of \xBD SE tax, and the \xA7 219(c) spousal-compensation rule is assumed satisfied on joint returns; disclosed. Pub 590-A groups qualifying surviving spouses with joint filers for the covered range (the statutory text says "joint return" \u2014 IRS guidance controls filing practice; disclosed). Not modeled, disclosed: the \xA7 219(g)(4) living-apart-all-year MFS exception (conservative), nondeductible-contribution basis (Form 8606), Roth IRAs, and the 6% excess-contribution excise.`
